  "teach": {
    "narration_en": "Three shapes that don't play by the usual rules. ة is taa marbuta — a hidden h, like in رَحْمَة (mercy). ى is alif maqsura — no dots, but it says a long 'aa' just like a regular alif, as in مُوسَى (Musa). آ is alif madda — a hamza stretched automatically to two counts right from the start of the word, as in آدَمْ (Adam).",
    "glyphs": ["رَحْمَة", "مُوسَى", "آدَمْ"],
    "focus_en": "ة sounds like h, ى sounds like a long alif, آ starts a word already stretched."
